+## Authentication and permissions
+
+Every request requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, matching an `apiKeys`
+record in the data. Missing, malformed, or unknown keys return 401 with code
+`unauthorized`; insufficient permission returns 403 with code `forbidden`.
+Both use the error shape below.
+
+Viewers may GET all routes except `/audit`. Cooks have the same read access
+and may POST `/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers may perform every operation.
+
+## Routes
+
+All existing routes and parameters are listed under Routes in `README.md`.
+`GET /audit` is manager-only and returns an array of entries newest first
+(reverse insertion order for equal times). Each successful data-changing
+request appends `{ time, keyName, method, path, status }` and saves it with
+the change. Reads, rejected requests, and failed operations add no entry.
+
